--TEST--
`$a = &$b;` is `E0701` in every position it can be written, never a panic — ADR 0031 § 2, ADR 0023
--FILE--
<?mwl
// MWL has no references at all: ADR 0031 § 2 removed by-reference capture, so
// no binding aliases another, and ADR 0023 makes the right-hand side a copy.
// So `= &` has no owner in either rule — a refusal, not a missing lowering.
int $b = 1;
int $a = 2;
$a = &$b;

// An element target takes the same answer, and takes it once: the `&` is
// refused before the write target is even considered.
array<int> $rows = ["0" => 1];
$rows["0"] = &$b;

// PHP's other spelling of the same thing, inside an expression rather than as
// a statement of its own.
int $c = ($a = &$b);
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
  --> %s:7:1
  |
7 | $a = &$b;
  | ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
  = help: MWL has no references: ADR 0031 § 2 removed by-reference capture and ADR 0023 makes this a copy, so drop the `&` — to share one mutable cell, hold it in an object and assign that

error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
   --> %s:12:1
   |
12 | $rows["0"] = &$b;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
   = help: MWL has no references: ADR 0031 § 2 removed by-reference capture and ADR 0023 makes this a copy, so drop the `&` — to share one mutable cell, hold it in an object and assign that

error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
   --> %s:16:11
   |
16 | int $c = ($a = &$b);
   |           ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
   = help: MWL has no references: ADR 0031 § 2 removed by-reference capture and ADR 0023 makes this a copy, so drop the `&` — to share one mutable cell, hold it in an object and assign that

error: aborting due to 3 errors
